--TEST--
inside the string literal a `require` takes as its path, the list is what the directory its text reaches holds, resolved against the document's own directory: each directory with a `/` after it and each `.nvs` file, spelled the way the disk spells them, and no other file — `rule:ide/completion-offers-only-what-the-compiler-derived`
--FILE--
<?nvs
require 'lib/<|>';
--FILE lib/User.nvs--
<?nvs
class User { }
--FILE lib/Models/Cart.nvs--
<?nvs
class Cart { }
--FILE lib/notes.txt--
notes
--REQUEST--
completion
--EXPECT--
Models/ folder
User.nvs file
